  "_readme": "Army maker data (/coc/tools/army-maker). Every unit the game can put in an army, with its in-game id (the number in a Copy Army link), housing space, the first Town Hall that unlocks it (th) and, for clan castle units, the first Town Hall that can receive it (ccTh). enabledTh lists the Town Halls the maker offers. Icons live in imageDir. Adding a new unit = adding one entry with its id from a real Copy Army link. Checked against the Clash of Clans wiki (Sep 30, 2026): every Town Hall's camp / spell / clan castle space, hero slots, and each unit's unlock Town Hall. Clan castle rules (ccTh) come from each unit's wiki page; Sky Wagon's is not stated there, so it is set to TH17 (the Town Hall that unlocks it), and Super Miner / Super Yeti stay at their boost Town Hall. The th18-army.json ... th9-army.json comps all fit these limits.",
